      "math_academy_id": "e-3987",
      "problem": "Find the value of $\\log_{3}{9}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite $9$ as a power of $3$ (the base of the logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n9 = 3^2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\log_{3}{9} = \\log_{3}(3^2).\n$$\n\nNow we can proceed as usual. The log of a power of the base equals the power itself:\n\n$$\n\\log_b(b^x) = x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $b = 3$ and $x = 2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\log_{3}(3^2) = 2.\n$$",
